{title: More Love to Thee}
{artist: Elizabeth P. Prentiss / William H. Doane}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}
{score: more-love-to-thee.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]More love to Thee, O [D]Christ
More [G]love to [C]Thee
Hear Thou the [G]prayer I [D]make
On [Em]bended [D]knee
This is my [G]earnest [C]plea
More love, O [G]Christ, to [D]Thee
More [G]love to [C]Thee, more [D]love to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Once earthly joy I [D]craved
Sought [G]peace and [C]rest
Now Thee a[G]lone I [D]seek
Give [Em]what is [D]best
This all my [G]prayer shall [C]be
More love, O [G]Christ, to [D]Thee
More [G]love to [C]Thee, more [D]love to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Let sorrow do its [D]work
Send [G]grief and [C]pain
Sweet are Thy [G]messen[D]gers
Sweet [Em]their re[D]frain
When they can [G]sing with [C]me
More love, O [G]Christ, to [D]Thee
More [G]love to [C]Thee, more [D]love to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Then shall my latest [D]breath
Whis[G]per Thy [C]praise
This be the [G]parting [D]cry
My [Em]heart shall [D]raise
This still its [G]prayer shall [C]be
More love, O [G]Christ, to [D]Thee
More [G]love to [C]Thee, more [D]love to [G]Thee
{end_of_verse}
